---
const rungs = ["said", "pointed", "walked", "ran", "reproduced"];
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-[1160px] px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
    <h2 class="text-balance font-display font-semibold text-[32px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-[52px] sm:leading-[1.02]">
      What a finding carries.
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-balance text-lg text-muted-foreground">
      Each finding records how it was checked, and the record travels with it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border p-8 sm:col-span-7">
      <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-2xl tracking-tight">An evidence rung</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-[52ch] text-base text-muted-foreground">
        A finding that was only said is labeled unproven. It is never posted as fact. The
        rung sets how far a finding travels.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        {
          rungs.map((rung, i) => (
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="h-2 rounded-full bg-accent"
                style={`width: ${(i + 1) * 36}px; opacity: ${0.35 + i * 0.16}`}
              />
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">{rung}</code>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border p-8 sm:col-span-5">
      <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight">Keep-biased machinery</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-muted-foreground">
        An anchor that might be valid is kept. Only a provably wrong anchor moves to the
        review body. A stale-SHA check and a double-post guard sit before the submit, and
        approving or requesting changes needs <code class="font-mono text-sm">--bind</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border p-8 sm:col-span-5">
      <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight">Stable memory</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-muted-foreground">
        Findings carry a signature that does not depend on line numbers, plus a status and
        a history. A re-review does not report a recorded finding again.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border p-8 sm:col-span-7">
      <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight">A machine surface</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-muted-foreground">
        Review verbs take <code class="font-mono text-sm">--json</code> and print one
        envelope. <code class="font-mono text-sm">report --sarif</code> writes SARIF 2.1.0.{" "}
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">calibrate</code> compares predictions with what
        happened to the PR.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
